  "goodToKnow": "Der Globus is a globe, and figuratively the world: rund um den Globus. The oldest surviving terrestrial globe, the Erdapfel (earth apple), was made by Martin Behaim in Nuremberg in 1492, just before Columbus returned, so it doesn't show the Americas. Global means global: die Globalisierung. Plural: die Globen or die Globusse."
